 "about_text": "Royale Projects is a Los Angeles gallery founded in 2008, dedicated to the history and ongoing development of abstraction in painting and sculpture, alongside artists whose work is rooted in Conceptualism. The gallery has presented debut exhibitions of artists such as Helen Pashgian, associated with the California Light & Space movement, and the last new works by Dennis Oppenheim. It has organized site-responsive desert projects in Joshua Tree, including collaborations with Andrea Zittel and Phillip K. Smith III. Its downtown Los Angeles Arts District space opened in 2015. The gallery participated in The Getty's Pacific Standard Time: LA/LA and represents the estate of Clinton Hill, contributing to renewed critical interest in his abstract paintings from the New York School.",
